  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "scene 005.5 — the tidecaller mountain chambers"
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "location: Tidecaller mountain interior"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 234"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Torhh, Senareth, Elyraen, Vairis, Olythae, Kyreth, Tidecaller Giants"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "focus: Torhh invites twenty Nephoretti into the mountain core to carve spiraling glass-smooth chambers and water-music channels that turn the mountain into a living instrument."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: Takes place 78 years after the first true pyramid in scene 005.4"
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: undecided"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "The Tidecallers finally invited Nephoretti into their mountain."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "It had taken over two centuries for the jade-green Giants to move beyond cautious coexistence into genuine trust."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "Torhh had been first, of course—the ocean-colored Giant whose curiosity had overcome instinct during those first terrible days."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "But convincing the entire Tidecaller faction required proof measured in generations, demonstrations of patience and non-harm that couldn't be faked or rushed."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "The invitation came through Torhh, who approached Senareth at the water's edge where they still sometimes worked patterns together."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "\"Our mountain."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "We wish to shape it."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "Make it home."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "But our communion alone is... crude."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "We lack precision."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "Will you help?\""
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "The mountain at the island's center had always been the Tidecallers' territory—the place they retreated to when fear overwhelmed curiosity, where they maintained their largest population concentration."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "Allowing Nephoretti inside meant allowing them into the heart of Tidecaller identity, into spaces where vulnerability couldn't be hidden."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "Senareth brought only a small group—Elyraen for their analytical precision, Vairis for practical engineering sense, Olythae for artistic vision, and Kyreth whose gentle nature had first broken through Torhh's fear."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "Twenty Nephoretti total, vastly outnumbered by the hundreds of Tidecallers who called the mountain home."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "The work took decades."
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "The Tidecallers wanted chambers—spaces carved from living rock that could serve as meditation halls, gathering places, storage for the few material possessions Giants maintained."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "But more than utility, they wanted beauty."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "They wanted their home to reflect the ocean they remembered even if conscious thought had forgotten, to carry the essence of coral forests and tidal rhythms into mountain stone."
  - line: 53
    type: narration
    text: "Nephoretti taught precision-shaping through consciousness-touch."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "Giants provided the raw power and scale."
  - line: 55
    type: narration
    text: "Together, they carved spiraling chambers that descended deep into the mountain's heart, their walls polished smooth as glass, their acoustic properties creating spaces where even whispered harmonics resonated with cathedral clarity."
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "Water channels threaded through the mountain—not for drinking, but for music."
  - line: 58
    type: narration
    text: "The Tidecallers directed underground streams through carved passages that made the entire structure sing when tide changed, when rain fell, when ocean currents shifted in the waters surrounding the island."
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "The mountain became instrument, playing harmonies that could be heard from the mainland when wind carried sound across the tidal causeway."
  - line: 61
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Torhh
    text: "\"This is what we build when fear doesn't rule us,\""
  - line: 63
    type: narration
    text: "The Tidecaller mountain became legend among the other Giant factions—proof that cooperation between species could create beauty beyond what either achieved alone."
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "Other groups requested Nephoretti assistance with their own territorial centers."
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "Mountain Giants wanted help carving meditation chambers at high altitudes."
  - line: 66
    type: narration
    text: "Desert Giants sought aid in shaping structures that could withstand sandstorms."
  - line: 67
    type: narration
    text: "Forest Giants asked for techniques to encourage living architecture—trees and stone growing together into organic fortifications."
  - line: 69
    type: narration
    text: "The Garden was no longer scattered experiments."
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "It was becoming civilization."
  - line: 72
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 74
    type: narration
    text: "year 312"

